## jt-portable-detect — auditd rules for execution from user-writable areas
##
## These turn on the only part of this pack that proves a program ran rather
## than that one was prepared. Manager rules 906210 and 906211 read the keys
## set here; without this file they never fire, and the file-based rules carry
## on working on their own.
##
## Install:
##
##     cp jt-portable.rules /etc/audit/rules.d/
##     augenrules --load          # or: service auditd restart
##     auditctl -l | grep jt_portable
##
## The agent picks the records up from /var/log/audit/audit.log, which the
## pack's agent.conf already reads.
##
## Cost. A -p x watch records an audit event per execution under that path.
## /tmp, /var/tmp and /dev/shm are quiet on a server, so the three enabled
## below are close to free. /home is not quiet on a multi-user or developer
## host -- every tool a person runs from their own directory is a record --
## so it ships commented out. Turn it on where the answer matters more than
## the volume, not everywhere by default.
##
## Note on ordering: if your /etc/audit/rules.d/ ends with a rule that sets
## the immutable flag (-e 2), place this file before it. Rules after -e 2 are
## refused until the next reboot, silently as far as the ruleset is concerned.

## Programs run from a temporary or memory filesystem. A binary here is
## either an installer doing its job or something that wants to leave no
## trace on disk, and rule 906211 treats it as the latter.
-w /tmp -p x -k jt_portable_tmpexec
-w /var/tmp -p x -k jt_portable_tmpexec
-w /dev/shm -p x -k jt_portable_tmpexec

## Programs run from removable media. Rare on a server, and the classic way
## a portable tool arrives on a workstation.
-w /media -p x -k jt_portable_exec
-w /mnt -p x -k jt_portable_exec
-w /run/media -p x -k jt_portable_exec

## Programs run out of the administrator's own directory.
-w /root -p x -k jt_portable_exec

## Programs run from any user's home directory. Accurate and noisy; see the
## note on cost above before enabling it.
# -w /home -p x -k jt_portable_exec
